v8: keep Stack::ObtainCurrentThreadStackReservedLimit out of Darwin builds.

Origin: EmberBSD (AI-assisted), not submitted upstream.
Source: Chromium electron-source tree under EmberBSD.
The EmberBSD BSD port moves the generic POSIX
ObtainCurrentThreadStackReservedLimit() outside the
!FREEBSD/!DARWIN/!AIX/!SOLARIS block so OpenBSD/NetBSD get it. That also
defined it for the macOS host toolchain, where platform-darwin.cc already
provides it, so ld64.lld fails linking torque with a duplicate symbol.
Guard the generic definition again for those OSes.

--- a/src/base/platform/platform-posix.cc	2026-10-28 02:18:35.760106322 +0300
+++ b/src/base/platform/platform-posix.cc	2026-10-28 02:18:35.772754208 +0300
@@ -1503,6 +1503,10 @@
 #endif  // !defined(V8_OS_FREEBSD) && !defined(V8_OS_DARWIN) &&
         // !defined(_AIX) && !defined(V8_OS_SOLARIS)
 
+// Darwin, FreeBSD, AIX and Solaris provide their own definition in
+// platform-<os>.cc; EmberBSD's BSD port only needs this one elsewhere.
+#if !defined(V8_OS_FREEBSD) && !defined(V8_OS_DARWIN) && !defined(_AIX) && \
+    !defined(V8_OS_SOLARIS)
 // static
 Stack::StackSlot Stack::ObtainCurrentThreadStackReservedLimit() {
 #if V8_OS_ZOS
@@ -1526,6 +1530,7 @@
   return base;
 #endif  // V8_OS_ZOS
 }
+#endif  // !V8_OS_FREEBSD && !V8_OS_DARWIN && !_AIX && !V8_OS_SOLARIS
 
 
 // static
